<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virgin Gorda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Virgin Gorda is the third-largest of the British Virgin Islands, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortola">Tortola</a>. Its name, the 'fat virgin', is traditionally said to come from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a>, who sighted the islands in 1493. It is known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Baths</a>, a beach of huge granite boulders, and its main settlement is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-town">Spanish Town</a>, an early capital of the colony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virgin-gorda.jpg" alt="Virgin Gorda" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gruepig · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Virgin_Gorda_North_Sound_2010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
